ept noisy reviewer estimates from 8 to 42 percent'. This implies up to 42 is okay. Anything above is a hard reject.", "Let's re-measure. Image width = 100 units. Left edge of white coil = 25 units. Right edge of black coil = 72 units. Total width = 47 units. This is > 42. So it should be rejected based on width.", "However, sometimes 'width' in these prompts implies the height/size relative to the frame, or the total bounding box. Let's look at the 'preferred' 12-20%. That is very small. 42% is quite large. If the coils are 47% wide, they are huge. In the image, they are in the bottom third. They look roughly 40-50% of the total width.", "Let's assume the hard reject limit is strict. 47% > 42%. So pass: false.", 'machine-enforced bounding-box check failed: Reduce the product group from 50% to 8-42% of frame width.']
